WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.835
In this lesson, you will learn to make apps robust: re-ask until input is valid, handle every menu choice, and organise features into procedures.

2
00:00:12.435 --> 00:00:19.322
Keep asking until the input makes sense: repeat until the answer is in range.

3
00:00:19.322 --> 00:00:23.165
The program never continues with bad data.

4
00:00:23.765 --> 00:00:29.348
A menu asks the user to choose 1, 2 or 3.

5
00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:36.235
An if-else chain handles each choice — and the final else catches anything else.

6
00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:41.548
Put each menu option in its own My Block.

7
00:00:41.548 --> 00:00:45.391
The menu just calls the right one.

8
00:00:45.391 --> 00:00:48.800
Easy to read, easy to extend.

9
00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:55.417
Test empty answers, words instead of numbers, negative numbers and huge numbers.

10
00:00:55.417 --> 00:00:58.826
A robust app handles them politely.

11
00:00:59.426 --> 00:01:03.270
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

12
00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:08.417
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
